@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature: OSB Product
	Testing OSB Product functionality.

Setup:
	* I get all passwords

Teardown:
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay OSB Product    |
	| A Liferay Server Product |
	* I tear down the following products
	| A Liferay OSB Product    |
	| A Liferay Server Product |

Scenario: Update and delete product
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Products updated on OSB that are no longer linked to a Koroneiki product key should also be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	Then I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"

Scenario: Update and delete product with external link
	Products updated on OSB that are no longer linked to a Koroneiki product key should also be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay OSB Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferayosb |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayOSB |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	Then I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"

Scenario: Update and delete product updated via Koroneiki
	Products updated via Koroneiki that are also updated on OSB that are no longer linked to a Koroneiki product key should also be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product"
	Then I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product"
	And I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"

Scenario: Attempt to delete linked product
	Products linked to Koroneiki should not be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay OSB Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |

Scenario: Attempt to delete linked product with external link
	Products with external links linked to Koroneiki should not be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay OSB Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferayosb |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayOSB |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" and the following values
	| Name                      | A Liferay OSB Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key     | Verify from name      |
	| External Link Domain      | liferayosb            |
	| External Link Entity Id   | 1234                  |
	| External Link Entity Name | LiferayOSB            |

Scenario: Attempt to delete linked product updated via Koroneiki
	Products updated via Koroneiki that are linked to Koroneiki should not be removable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki with the name "A Liferay Server Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Server Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |
	And I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"

Scenario: Add back deleted product
	Products removed from OSB should be able to be added back via OSB

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	And I add a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay OSB Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |

Scenario: Add back deleted updated product
	Updated products removed from OSB should be able to be added back via OSB

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product"
	And I add a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Server Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |

Scenario: Attempt to delete added back product
	Products removed and added back via OSB should not be removable via OSB

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	And I add a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product |
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay OSB Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |

Scenario: Attempt to delete updated and added back product
	Updated products removed and added back via OSB should not be removable via OSB

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product" with the following values
	| Koroneiki Product Key | KOR-123 |
	And I delete a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product"
	And I add a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product |
	And I attempt to delete a product linked to Koroneiki with the name "A Liferay Server Product"
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Server Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |